2
00:03:39,544 --> 00:03:44,500
For aeons, light and dark have fought ceaselessly,

3
00:03:44,500 --> 00:03:48,200
for dominion over the world.

4
00:03:48,200 --> 00:03:56,800
Whispers echo of a dark lord, whose insidious grip on the realm is marked by insatiable lust,

5
00:03:57,000 --> 00:04:03,400
twisted jealousy, ravenous greed, unrelenting vanity, and possessive manipulation.

6
00:04:03,400 --> 00:04:16,200
A group of adventurers rose to face this threat with hidden wishes of secrets and shadows untold.

7
00:04:16,800 --> 00:04:19,400
First, there was Namu,

8
00:04:19,400 --> 00:04:28,000
quick as an owl in the night, a thrill-seeking thief she was, who hunted in the fringes of society.

9
00:04:28,800 --> 00:04:41,200
Next was Cora, a passionate chronomancer and hostess, whose connections to this world felt as thin as the threads of time she manipulated to build her harem.

10
00:04:42,500 --> 00:04:54,300
Vailin was a guardian of nature whose sweet, charming exterior belied her true nature.

11
00:04:54,800 --> 00:05:03,456
Descended from the heavens, Irisa brought tidings of doom, her innocent...

12
00:05:04,408 --> 00:05:07,308
Clumsy demeanor stood in contrast to her

13
00:05:07,308 --> 00:05:10,808
perfectionist tendencies.

14
00:05:12,808 --> 00:05:14,508
Lastly, Hexa,

15
00:05:14,808 --> 00:05:18,208
a bard who had yet to find her spotlight.

16
00:05:18,408 --> 00:05:21,208
Dazzling were her performances,

17
00:05:21,208 --> 00:05:27,508
whilst her silent dreams of recognition awed e'er her heart.

18
00:05:29,108 --> 00:05:33,808
On a warm summer night, amidst the flickering candlelight of the Singing Shark,

19
00:05:33,908 --> 00:05:38,208
in, they found their fates intertwined

20
00:05:38,208 --> 00:05:47,108
with that of a malevolent dark lord, whose shadow slowly consumed everything in their path.

21
00:06:00,208 --> 00:06:03,908
Hey Faelyn, how dost thou cope with death?

22
00:06:04,008 --> 00:06:06,608
The fear thereof, I mean.

23
00:06:07,308 --> 00:06:13,508
Tending to my plants helps stave off the looming specter of the void, if but for a spell.

24
00:06:14,208 --> 00:06:15,308
Plants, huh?

25
00:06:15,608 --> 00:06:16,708
Try them once.

26
00:06:16,808 --> 00:06:17,908
Kill them all.

27
00:06:18,208 --> 00:06:20,808
Yes, I'm destined to bring death one way or another.

28
00:06:21,308 --> 00:06:26,508
Mayhaps thou art stick to nursing pines rather than plants, Hexa.

29
00:06:26,808 --> 00:06:28,708
Nature's children are precious.

30
00:06:28,808 --> 00:06:30,608
Thy liver is not.

31
00:06:31,408 --> 00:06:33,608
I'll drink to that!

32
00:06:36,908 --> 00:06:40,408
Comely maiden, might I follow thee home?

33
00:06:40,408 --> 00:06:43,008
Twice my mother's wish that I follow my dreams.

34
00:06:44,108 --> 00:06:45,808
A fine distraction, Kora.

35
00:06:47,208 --> 00:06:50,008
Namu is so clever, isn't she?

36
00:06:51,108 --> 00:06:54,808
Thou mistakest me for thine accomplice, Namu.

37
00:06:55,108 --> 00:06:58,808
Canst thou not see I'm trying to work my magic here?

38
00:06:59,208 --> 00:07:02,708
Already resorting to time magic to ensnare thy quarry?

39
00:07:03,008 --> 00:07:07,208
Tush, pretty turn of phrase. I hardly need magic to court a maiden fair,

40
00:07:07,408 --> 00:07:10,608
merely my unending charm.

41
00:07:10,808 --> 00:07:12,908
Hast thou not enough trinkets already?

42
00:07:13,108 --> 00:07:16,108
I take no more than I need to survive, I promise.

43
00:07:18,208 --> 00:07:20,808
Would seem at least someone is getting lucky tonight.

44
00:07:21,308 --> 00:07:23,308
Let me see. What'd you get?

45
00:07:29,108 --> 00:07:31,108
Fie! Here comes the guard. That is my cue to vanish.

46
00:07:32,808 --> 00:07:38,008
Namu, methinks the guard doth not arrive bathed in heavenly light.

47
00:07:39,508 --> 00:07:41,408
Greetings, esteemed patrons.

48
00:07:41,608 --> 00:07:45,808
I seek stout-hearted souls to accompany me on a dangerous...

49
00:07:50,008 --> 00:07:51,308
How charming.

50
00:07:54,908 --> 00:07:57,408
Tis is not a journey to be taken lightly.

51
00:07:57,608 --> 00:08:00,008
The darkness grows stronger by the day.

52
00:08:00,208 --> 00:08:04,208
Join me, and thy deepest wish will be granted.

53
00:08:04,508 --> 00:08:06,108
Deepest wish?

54
00:08:06,308 --> 00:08:07,908
Sounds like a ruse to me.

55
00:08:08,008 --> 00:08:09,108
What think you?

56
00:08:09,608 --> 00:08:10,808
Might be.

57
00:08:11,008 --> 00:08:12,508
But what if it's not?

58
00:08:13,908 --> 00:08:15,208
Oi, shiny lady!

59
00:08:15,508 --> 00:08:17,208
Where's ol' I? So go on,

60
00:08:17,508 --> 00:08:19,508
spin us your tale.

61
00:08:20,108 --> 00:08:21,408
How can we trust thee?

62
00:08:21,608 --> 00:08:23,408
Who art thou, anyway?

63
00:08:23,808 --> 00:08:26,208
I understand your skepticism.

64
00:08:26,508 --> 00:08:29,208
In times like these, we all have our doubts.

65
00:08:29,808 --> 00:08:36,408
My name is IRyS. I descended from the celestial realm on a holy quest to end the dark lord's reign.

66
00:08:37,208 --> 00:08:42,508
'Tis foretold that by vanquishing the dark lord, one's heart's desires will be granted.

67
00:08:43,608 --> 00:08:46,508
What dost thou mean by our heart's desire?

68
00:08:47,008 --> 00:08:50,108
Each of you carries within you a longing that drives you.

69
00:08:50,408 --> 00:08:54,108
This quest can make those aspirations a reality.

70
00:08:55,208 --> 00:08:57,108
Have you any proof?

71
00:09:05,008 --> 00:09:06,108
There.

72
00:09:06,908 --> 00:09:08,808
Now dost thou believe me?

73
00:09:09,508 --> 00:09:10,708
Kora, what is wrong?

74
00:09:10,808 --> 00:09:13,508
Thou lookest like thou hast seen a ghost.

75
00:09:14,008 --> 00:09:18,308
What witch craft hast thou wrought upon her, foul enchantress?

76
00:09:18,908 --> 00:09:20,208
I only showed her the truth.

77
00:09:22,408 --> 00:09:23,808
Is this the future?

78
00:09:26,208 --> 00:09:28,208
Oh, one moment. I shall return forthwith.

79
00:09:31,808 --> 00:09:33,008
Indeed, it...

80
00:09:33,108 --> 00:09:35,008
Where'd she go?

81
00:09:35,908 --> 00:09:37,208
Ah, she sha'n't be gone long.

82
00:09:37,408 --> 00:09:39,008
Watch, she'll turn anon.

83
00:09:42,108 --> 00:09:44,008
Though it may beggar belief,

84
00:09:44,208 --> 00:09:45,808
IRyS speaks the truth.

85
00:09:46,008 --> 00:09:48,208
Our wishes can be granted.

86
00:09:49,008 --> 00:09:51,308
Truly? We can wish for anything?

87
00:09:52,308 --> 00:09:53,208
Any wish.

88
00:09:53,808 --> 00:09:54,808
Any wish?

89
00:09:54,808 --> 00:09:55,908
Well then,

90
00:09:56,008 --> 00:09:58,008
wherefore do we tarry? Let us away!

91
00:10:10,086 --> 00:10:13,006
(諦めない強さなら)
(If you have unyielding strength,)

92
00:10:15,816 --> 00:10:18,796
(明日が見えないのなら)
(If you cannot see tomorrow,)

93
00:10:32,236 --> 00:10:37,416
僕らは迷ってた 真っ暗狭い部屋
We were lost in a pitch-black, narrow room,

94
00:10:37,856 --> 00:10:43,016
僕らはあがいてた 光差すほう
We were struggling toward the shining light.

95
00:10:43,956 --> 00:10:49,356
不安やしがらみは 大きく膨らんで
Anxiety and entanglements swelled up large,

96
00:10:49,856 --> 00:10:54,556
襲いかかる 逃げ場はない 差し伸べる手も
Closing in with nowhere to run, even the hands reached out—

97
00:10:54,956 --> 00:10:59,956
嫌というほどに 繰り返して
Repeated to the point of disgust,

98
00:11:00,956 --> 00:11:06,456
それでも まだまだ 与えるのか
Yet still, will you give us more?

99
00:11:06,756 --> 00:11:08,756
試練の日々よ
Oh, days of trial!

100
00:11:09,556 --> 00:11:14,756
諦めない強さなら それなりに平等だけど
If you have unyielding strength, it's fair in its own way, but

101
00:11:15,756 --> 00:11:20,756
振り絞ったよ 今にもダメになりそう
I squeezed out all my strength, about to break any second.

102
00:11:21,256 --> 00:11:31,856
そんなとき ふと見上げた 先駆者たちの言葉には 同じ香り 感じたんだ
At that moment, glancing up, in the words of those who came before, I felt the same scent.

103
00:11:42,056 --> 00:11:47,156
僕らは夢を見た さまざま 思い思い
We dreamed various dreams, each as we pleased,

104
00:11:47,856 --> 00:11:52,756
僕らは賭けてみた お互いに全て
We placed our bets on everything, mutually.

105
00:11:53,256 --> 00:11:58,756
勝率や現実 ときには振り払って
Shaking off win rates and reality at times,

106
00:11:59,156 --> 00:12:04,456
泣けばいい 悔めばいい 途中経過さ
It's fine to cry, fine to regret, it's just along the way.

107
00:12:04,756 --> 00:12:10,356
夢中で息荒く 走り続け
Running on breathlessly in a dream,

108
00:12:10,656 --> 00:12:18,656
気づけば無数の仲間たちに 支えられながら
Before I knew it, supported by countless comrades—

109
00:12:19,756 --> 00:12:24,956
明日が見えないのなら その方角は間違いさ
If you cannot see tomorrow, that direction is mistaken.

110
00:12:25,756 --> 00:12:30,856
一呼吸置いて ゼロからの近道もある
Take a breath; there's also a shortcut from zero.

111
00:12:31,156 --> 00:12:42,856
簡単じゃないことでも 複雑に絡まる前に どうか一度 見せにおいで
Even if it's not easy, before it gets tangled up complexly, please, show it to us once.

112
00:12:51,956 --> 00:12:55,956
出会ったんだ
We met,

113
00:12:57,756 --> 00:13:01,956
魅かれたんだ
We were drawn in,

114
00:13:03,756 --> 00:13:08,456
それが奇跡
That is a miracle.

115
00:13:09,756 --> 00:13:14,456
君にありがとう
Thank you to you.

116
00:13:18,956 --> 00:13:24,756
きっと思いや強さなら それなりに平等だけど
Surely, if you have unyielding strength, it's fair in its own way, but

117
00:13:25,756 --> 00:13:30,756
振り絞ったよ 今にもダメになりそう
I squeezed out all my strength, about to break any second.

118
00:13:31,156 --> 00:13:38,956
そんなとき ふと見上げた 先駆者たちの言葉には 頼らない 歌うよ
At that moment, glancing up, in the words of those who came before, not relying on them, I will sing!

119
00:13:39,756 --> 00:13:44,956
明日が見えないのなら その方角は間違いさ
If you cannot see tomorrow, that direction is mistaken.

120
00:13:45,756 --> 00:13:50,756
一呼吸置いて ゼロからの近道もある
Take a breath; there's also a shortcut from zero.

121
00:13:51,156 --> 00:14:04,956
簡単じゃないことでも 複雑に絡まる前に どうか一度 見せにおいで
Even if it's not easy, before it gets tangled up complexly, please, show it to us once.

122
00:14:37,081 --> 00:14:40,361
Quite the jig thou didst dance back at the tavern.

123
00:14:40,761 --> 00:14:44,831
Was it to charm people or to scare away crows? I couldn't tell.

124
00:14:45,091 --> 00:14:50,371
A brazen stone to cast when none would countenance you without your magic.

125
00:14:51,031 --> 00:14:55,881
You're both very charming, but not as lovely as Namu.

126
00:14:56,431 --> 00:14:57,021
Huh?

127
00:14:57,081 --> 00:14:58,031
Lovely, you say?

128
00:14:58,231 --> 00:15:00,441
Is the moon not beautiful tonight?

129
00:15:00,531 --> 00:15:01,221
Uh...

130
00:15:02,231 --> 00:15:07,011
Although we ought not linger,

131
00:15:07,111 --> 00:15:11,961
rumor has it that an evil hag liveth in these parts,

132
00:15:12,111 --> 00:15:16,711
and now whet her appetite, like the flesh of adventurers.

133
00:15:17,033 --> 00:15:19,713
What art thou hiding, she thinks?

134
00:15:20,033 --> 00:15:23,713
What dost thou not want us to know about these woods?

135
00:15:23,933 --> 00:15:26,643
Tell us more about this hag.

136
00:15:27,013 --> 00:15:31,063
Aye, a frightful yawn doth excite my spirit!

137
00:15:32,063 --> 00:15:34,793
Canst thou all see she speaketh false?

138
00:15:38,013 --> 00:15:42,313
Gumi and her friend Darla were adventurers who gathered fruit in these woods.

139
00:15:42,413 --> 00:15:48,383
Gumi had heard of a trove of berries hidden deep in the forest, so they ventured in and found a grove untouched by man or beast.

140
00:15:49,013 --> 00:15:55,893
They began picking the berries in pure bliss, that is, until they heard a loud, snapping and crunching sound.

141
00:16:00,243 --> 00:16:01,783
What was that?

142
00:16:02,283 --> 00:16:10,883
They looked around, but saw nothing. Spooked by the unnatural sound, they decided to leave, but twas too late. They lost track of time.

143
00:16:11,293 --> 00:16:17,813
Night had fallen and darkness shrouded the woods. They split up and marked their path with berries.

144
00:16:18,203 --> 00:16:24,223
After some time, Gumi heard a scream followed by a bone-chilling crunch.

145
00:16:24,473 --> 00:16:33,343
Gumi ran down the berry trail with all the haste she could muster. The berries underfoot began to ooze a strange, red substance. It seeped into the ground.

146
00:16:33,693 --> 00:16:42,763
Each stain bigger than the last. Breathless, she came upon a large puddle of red, and in the centre, a pile of teeth.

147
00:16:43,433 --> 00:16:48,813
Frozen in horror, she looked up and beheld a grotesque hag looming over her,

148
00:16:49,013 --> 00:16:55,213
Darla's hair hanging from her mouth. Before she could react, the hag lunged!

149
00:16:56,093 --> 00:16:59,313
I'll mean to rob us of any chance of peaceful slumber?
Dost thou mean to rob us of any chance of peaceful slumber?

150
00:17:00,033 --> 00:17:02,493
Merely trying to keep you all on your toes.

151
00:17:03,283 --> 00:17:06,293
It's working. I don't think I'll sleep a wink tonight.

152
00:17:08,043 --> 00:17:13,143
Let us abscond from this place, starting to feel like we're being watched.

153
00:17:14,073 --> 00:17:17,843
None of you belong here.
An unwise choice. None of you belong here.

154
00:17:52,208 --> 00:17:57,518
ようこそ 深い森の奥
Welcome to the depths of the forest

155
00:17:58,148 --> 00:18:02,508
珍しい お客さんね
Such unusual guests

156
00:18:03,038 --> 00:18:08,618
悪いけど ここから先では
Sorry, but from here on out

157
00:18:08,948 --> 00:18:14,108
森でのマナーがあるの
There are rules to the forest

158
